How can I dynamically generate a list of five virtual classroom topics using PHP code, with each topic containing at least three letters from the word "ONLINE"? The topics should be displayed as a bulleted list on an HTML page.
Here's a sample PHP code that can achieve this:
<?php
$topics = array();
for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++) {
  $topic = '';
  $letters = str_shuffle('ONLINE');
  $count = 0;
  while ($count < 3) {
    $letter = substr($letters, $count, 1);
    if (!strstr($topic, $letter)) {
      $topic .= $letter;
      $count++;
    }
  }
  $topics[] = $topic;
}
echo '<ul>';
foreach ($topics as $topic) {
  echo '<li>' . $topic . '</li>';
}
echo '</ul>';
?>
This code generates five random topics, each containing at least three letters from "ONLINE", and stores them in an array. It then loops through the array and outputs the topics as a bulleted list on the HTML page.

